  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>Between Monaco and Menton, Golfe Bleu beach occupies the Cabbé cove: a pebble beach between cliffs and turquoise sea, reached mainly on foot via the Sentier Le Corbusier from the train station, according to the town hall.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>Several guides cite a dog-reserved area on this beach, but we found no official source confirming it: the "Les plages" page of the Roquebrune-Cap-Martin town hall doesn't mention dogs. Guides also disagree on its location: a Cannes tourist office document (2023) places it at the eastern end, on the promenade Robert Schumann, dogs on a leash, while other sources mention the western end, and another even claims the town's beaches are banned to dogs. Call the town hall before coming specifically for this beach.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: Monaco, right next door, has no beach open to dogs in this guide — the Pointe des Douaniers in Cap-d'Ail or Hawaï beach in Menton are better-documented alternatives.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The Menton dog beach is just a few kilometres east, a good option if you're combining several Riviera spots in the same day.</p>
